{
  "manufacturer": "Inovance",
  "manufacturer_slug": "inovance",
  "model": "MD200 series compact AC drive",
  "model_slug": "md200",
  "short_model": "MD200",
  "aliases": [
    "MD200",
    "MD200T",
    "MD200S",
    "MD200-NC",
    "Inovance MD200"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Inovance MD200 single- and three-phase compact drives using the RS-485 Modbus RTU port, per user guide 19012113 rev. C02.",
  "summary": "Inovance's compact general-purpose drive for small machines, fans and pumps. Its RS-485 port speaks Modbus RTU. Speed is written as a signed percentage to 1000H, run commands go to 2000H, status and fault sit at 3000H and 8000H, and every parameter (F/A groups at FxxxH/AxxxH, U0 monitors at 70xxH) has its own hex address. This map covers the control registers, the main U0 monitors and the FD communication parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are hex and go on the wire unchanged: the guide reads F0-10 with 01 03 F0 0A ..., writes AC-16 with 01 06 4C 10 ... and sets the frequency with 01 06 10 00 .... A parameter's address is its group code (F0H-FFH, A0H-AFH, 70H-7FH for U0-UF) followed by its number in hex."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "MD200 Series General-Purpose AC Drive User Guide",
    "doc_number": "19012113 C02",
    "revision_date": "2023-01",
    "url": "https://inovance.eu/fileadmin/downloads/Manuals/EN/MD200/MD200_User_Guide_EN_C02_19012113.PDF",
    "pages": "pp. 81-85 (6.1 communication data address), p. 285 and pp. 314-317 (F9-14 fault list), pp. 331-333 (F0, FD groups), pp. 339-342 (U0 group)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are single 16-bit words. Scales follow the decimals printed in each parameter's range; the guide's read example returns 13 88 (5000) for F0-10 = 50.00 Hz.",
    "To write F-group parameters without storing them in EEPROM, replace the leading F with 0 (F0-16 -> 0010H); A-group parameters use 4x instead of Ax.",
    "Left out: U0-14 and U0-19 (decimal places set by F7-12), U0-61 (drive state code, no value table), U0-69 (printed Int16 with a 0.00-655.35 Hz range), single-phase-only monitors (U0-12, U0-13, U0-24, U0-35, U0-65, U0-78) and reserved rows.",
    "Fault code 6 is printed with the same text as code 3 ('Overcurrent during deceleration'), so its real meaning is unclear. Reserved fault codes are omitted.",
    "2000H, 2001H, 2002H and 1000H are write-only; 2001H bits other than relay 1 are reserved on MD200."
  ],
